    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0851" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.2553/10–1850: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-18T16:00:00-05:00">October 18, 1950—4
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>281. At request of President Gomez who stated he was dissatisfied with existing
                    petroleum laws, petroleum companies were invited to make suggestions to be
                    incorporated in new petroleum law which would attract foreign capital. After
                    industry meeting Monday to formulate views, petroleum group met yesterday and
                    today in continuing series of meetings with Minister Mines [and]
                        Petroleum<anchor n="1" xml:id="d436-f1"/> to present industry views.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d436-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d436-f1" n="1" xml:id="d436-f1-content">
                <p>Manuel Carvajal Sinisterra.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d436-f2" n="2" xml:id="d436-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 353 from Bogota, November 15, 1950, Ambassador Beaulac reported in
                    part the Government had signed a new petroleum law which, among other
                    provisions, removed the limit on the number of concessions a single company
                    could hold and provided incentives for early drilling. (821.2553/11–1550)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
